      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(the relevant area) at the time of that cessation or within the next 6 months",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(the declaration takes effect at the time of that cessation)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-24a-ss-1-logic-argumentation-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Applicable",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Justification for declaration",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a person (the former provider) ceases to be a universal service provider for a particular area (the relevant area))",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(another person (the current provider) is declared, by declaration that takes effect at the time of that cessation or within the next 6 months, to be a universal service provider for some or all of that area)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-24a-ss-1-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Applicable",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Declaration affects former provider's obligations",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(the declaration referred to in paragraph (a) may be a declaration made before, at the same time as, or after the time when the former provider ceases to be a universal service provider)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(the former provider is required to provide services after cessation)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-24a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24A(2) Former universal service provider may be required to provide",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-24a-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The current provider may, by written notice given to the former\nprovider, require the former provider to give to the current provider\nspecified information of the kind referred to in subsection (3). A\nnotice of this kind cannot be given more than 6 months after:\n\n(a) if paragraph (1)(a) applies:\n\n(i) the later of the day on which the declaration referred to\nin paragraph (1)(a) was made and the day on which that\ndeclaration takes effect; or\n\n(ii) if both of those things happen on the same day—that\nday; or\n\n(b) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—the day on which the former\nprovider ceases to be a universal service provider for the\nrelevant area.\nNote:\nIf paragraph (1)(a) applies, a notice under this subsection may be\ngiven by the current provider even if the declaration referred to in that\nparagraph has not yet taken effect.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The current provider may, by written notice given to the former\nprovider, require the former provider to give to the current provider\nspecified information of the kind referred to in subsection (3). A\nnotice of this kind cannot be given more than 6 months after:\n\n(a) if paragraph (1)(a) applies:\n\n(i) the later of the day on which the declaration referred to\nin paragraph (1)(a) was made and the day on which that\ndeclaration takes effect; or\n\n(ii) if both of those things happen on the same day—that\nday; or\n\n(b) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—the day on which the former\nprovider ceases to be a universal service provider for the\nrelevant area.\nNote:\nIf paragraph (1)(a) applies, a notice under this subsection may be\ngiven by the current provider even if the declaration referred to in that\nparagraph has not yet taken effect.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-24a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-24a-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-24a-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e1905cfe9576a021df24961ef106de5f9e458446eb7eb63ca4eedf0f55605d94",
      "skos:note": "Current provider may require former universal service provider to provide specified information.",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-24a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24A(2) Former universal service provider may be required to provide",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The current provider may, by written notice given to the former\nprovider, require the former provider to give to the current provider\nspecified information of the kind referred to in subsection (3). A\nnotice of this kind cannot be given more than 6 months after:\n\n(a) if paragraph (1)(a) applies:\n\n(i) the later of the day on which the declaration referred to\nin paragraph (1)(a) was made and the day on which that\ndeclaration takes effect; or\n\n(ii) if both of those things happen on the same day—that\nday; or\n\n(b) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—the day on which the former\nprovider ceases to be a universal service provider for the\nrelevant area.\nNote:\nIf paragraph (1)(a) applies, a notice under this subsection may be\ngiven by the current provider even if the declaration referred to in that\nparagraph has not yet taken effect."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-24a-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
