      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If a requirement made by a notice under subsection (2) is\nreasonable, the former provider must comply with the requirement\nas soon as practicable after receiving the notice. However, if the\nrequirement is unreasonable, the former provider does not have to\ncomply with it.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments relating to the universal service regime",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If a requirement made by a notice under subsection (2) is\nreasonable, the former provider must comply with the requirement\nas soon as practicable after receiving the notice. However, if the\nrequirement is unreasonable, the former provider does not have to\ncomply with it.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments relating to the universal service regime",
      "values:partOf": {
