    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26f-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": ">=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Time of cessation must be within the next 6 months",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(declaration takes effect at the time of that cessation or within the next 6 months)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(cessation must occur before declaration takes effect)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26f-ss-1-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "<=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Current provider was also a digital data service provider for some or all of the relevant area",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(former provider ceases to be a digital data service provider and another person continues after that cessation)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(current provider must continue providing services for some or all of that area)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26f-ss-1-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MAY",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Declaration may be made before, at the same time as, or after the time when the former provider ceases to be a digital data service provider",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(declaration referred to in paragraph (a) may be a declaration made before, at the same time as, or after the time when the former provider ceases to be a digital data service provider)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(declaration is not required to take effect immediately)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26f-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26F(2) Former digital data service provider may be required to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-26f-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The current provider may, by written notice given to the former\nprovider, require the former provider to give to the current provider\nspecified information of the kind referred to in subsection (3). A\nnotice of this kind cannot be given more than 6 months after:\n\n(a) if paragraph (1)(a) applies:\n\n(i) the later of the day on which the declaration referred to\nin paragraph (1)(a) was made and the day on which that\ndeclaration takes effect; or\n\n(ii) if both of those things happen on the same day—that\nday; or\n\n(b) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—the day on which the former\nprovider ceases to be a digital data service provider for the\nrelevant area.\n\nAmendments relating to the universal service regime  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 1) 2000\nNo. 95, 2000            13\nNote:\nIf paragraph (1)(a) applies, a notice under this subsection may be\ngiven by the current provider even if the declaration referred to in that\nparagraph has not yet taken effect.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The current provider may, by written notice given to the former\nprovider, require the former provider to give to the current provider\nspecified information of the kind referred to in subsection (3). A\nnotice of this kind cannot be given more than 6 months after:\n\n(a) if paragraph (1)(a) applies:\n\n(i) the later of the day on which the declaration referred to\nin paragraph (1)(a) was made and the day on which that\ndeclaration takes effect; or\n\n(ii) if both of those things happen on the same day—that\nday; or\n\n(b) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—the day on which the former\nprovider ceases to be a digital data service provider for the\nrelevant area.\n\nAmendments relating to the universal service regime  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 1) 2000\nNo. 95, 2000            13\nNote:\nIf paragraph (1)(a) applies, a notice under this subsection may be\ngiven by the current provider even if the declaration referred to in that\nparagraph has not yet taken effect.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26f"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26f-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26f-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9a72083a6e3d077d0bef2daaba008aa8aaba23f72a5d219807ce674f91dbc388",
      "skos:note": "Current provider may require former provider to provide specified information.",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-26f-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26F(2) Former digital data service provider may be required to",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The current provider may, by written notice given to the former\nprovider, require the former provider to give to the current provider\nspecified information of the kind referred to in subsection (3). A\nnotice of this kind cannot be given more than 6 months after:\n\n(a) if paragraph (1)(a) applies:\n\n(i) the later of the day on which the declaration referred to\nin paragraph (1)(a) was made and the day on which that\ndeclaration takes effect; or\n\n(ii) if both of those things happen on the same day—that\nday; or\n\n(b) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—the day on which the former\nprovider ceases to be a digital data service provider for the\nrelevant area.\n\nAmendments relating to the universal service regime  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 1) 2000\nNo. 95, 2000            13\nNote:\nIf paragraph (1)(a) applies, a notice under this subsection may be\ngiven by the current provider even if the declaration referred to in that\nparagraph has not yet taken effect."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26f-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
