    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26f-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26F(4) Former digital data service provider may be required to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-26f-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If a requirement made by a notice under subsection (2) is\nreasonable, the former provider must comply with the requirement\nas soon as practicable after receiving the notice. However, if the\nrequirement is unreasonable, the former provider does not have to\ncomply with it.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If a requirement made by a notice under subsection (2) is\nreasonable, the former provider must comply with the requirement\nas soon as practicable after receiving the notice. However, if the\nrequirement is unreasonable, the former provider does not have to\ncomply with it.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26f"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26f-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26f-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26f-ss-4-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dc06b4aff3fecf4b5e95c07eedd87cc41ddf3ce18074143130bae6894632c711",
      "skos:note": "Former digital data service provider must comply with reasonable requirements.",
      "dc:description": "as soon as practicable after receiving the notice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-26f-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26F(4) Former digital data service provider may be required to",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If a requirement made by a notice under subsection (2) is\nreasonable, the former provider must comply with the requirement\nas soon as practicable after receiving the notice. However, if the\nrequirement is unreasonable, the former provider does not have to\ncomply with it."
    },
