      "cml:logicSummary": "Section 486 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 implies that Minister's powers are not limited by subsection (1F)",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Subsection (1F)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Minister's powers under section 486 of the Telecommunications Act 1997"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-18-2-ss-1j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "18(1J) Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-18-2-ss-1j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(1J) If:\n\n(a) the Minister has received advice under subsection (1F) about\na proposed determination or variation; and\n\n(b) the determination or variation is not made in accordance with\nthe advice;\nthe Minister must:\n\n(c) publish his or her reasons for departing from the advice in the\nGazette within 14 days after making the determination; and\n\n(d) cause copies of his or her reasons for departing from the\nadvice to be laid before each House of the Parliament within\n5 sitting days of that House after making the determination.",
      "skos:definition": "(1J) If:\n\n(a) the Minister has received advice under subsection (1F) about\na proposed determination or variation; and\n\n(b) the determination or variation is not made in accordance with\nthe advice;\nthe Minister must:\n\n(c) publish his or her reasons for departing from the advice in the\nGazette within 14 days after making the determination; and\n\n(d) cause copies of his or her reasons for departing from the\nadvice to be laid before each House of the Parliament within\n5 sitting days of that House after making the determination.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-18-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-18-2-ss-1j-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-18-2-ss-1j-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0dd3f8a6ad5a087c91b390c6f7784885fb7e68f37aa74b77bc9e3eb3a65b180c",
      "skos:note": "Publish reasons for departing from advice within 14 days and lay copies before Parliament.",
      "dc:description": "Reasons for departure"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-18-2-ss-1j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18(1J) Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "(1J) If:\n\n(a) the Minister has received advice under subsection (1F) about\na proposed determination or variation; and\n\n(b) the determination or variation is not made in accordance with\nthe advice;\nthe Minister must:\n\n(c) publish his or her reasons for departing from the advice in the\nGazette within 14 days after making the determination; and\n\n(d) cause copies of his or her reasons for departing from the\nadvice to be laid before each House of the Parliament within\n5 sitting days of that House after making the determination."
    },
