    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-83",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "83 New subsections 20(4) and (5) and old subsections 20(5)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-83"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "to (8)\n(1)\nSubsection 20(4) of the amended Act applies in relation to declarations\nreferred to in that subsection that are made on or after the\ncommencement.\n(2)\nSubsection 20(5) of the amended Act applies in relation to declarations\nmade before, on or after the commencement.\n(3)\nSubsection 20(5) of the old Act continues to apply in relation to a\ndeclaration made before the commencement as if the subsection had not\nbeen repealed.\n(4)\nSubsection 20(6) of the old Act continues to apply to a revocation made\nbefore the commencement as if the subsection had not been repealed.\n(5)\nIf subsection 20(7) or (8) of the old Act applied to 2 declarations (an\noriginal declaration and a fresh declaration) made before the\ncommencement, but the fresh declaration had not taken effect, and the\noriginal declaration had not ceased to have effect, under that subsection\nby the commencement, that subsection continues to apply to those\ndeclarations as if it had not been repealed.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments relating to the universal service regime",
      "skos:definition": "to (8)\n(1)\nSubsection 20(4) of the amended Act applies in relation to declarations\nreferred to in that subsection that are made on or after the\ncommencement.\n(2)\nSubsection 20(5) of the amended Act applies in relation to declarations\nmade before, on or after the commencement.\n(3)\nSubsection 20(5) of the old Act continues to apply in relation to a\ndeclaration made before the commencement as if the subsection had not\nbeen repealed.\n(4)\nSubsection 20(6) of the old Act continues to apply to a revocation made\nbefore the commencement as if the subsection had not been repealed.\n(5)\nIf subsection 20(7) or (8) of the old Act applied to 2 declarations (an\noriginal declaration and a fresh declaration) made before the\ncommencement, but the fresh declaration had not taken effect, and the\noriginal declaration had not ceased to have effect, under that subsection\nby the commencement, that subsection continues to apply to those\ndeclarations as if it had not been repealed.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments relating to the universal service regime",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-83-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-83-logic-alleninterval-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eb544e59db88e69c2a7cce6e497485ea5d862e95148baefd784c39e527b7ab76",
      "skos:note": "Applicability of old and new subsections of Act 20(4) and (5)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-83",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "83 New subsections 20(4) and (5) and old subsections 20(5)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 25,
      "values:originalText": "to (8)\n(1)\nSubsection 20(4) of the amended Act applies in relation to declarations\nreferred to in that subsection that are made on or after the\ncommencement.\n(2)\nSubsection 20(5) of the amended Act applies in relation to declarations\nmade before, on or after the commencement.\n(3)\nSubsection 20(5) of the old Act continues to apply in relation to a\ndeclaration made before the commencement as if the subsection had not\nbeen repealed.\n(4)\nSubsection 20(6) of the old Act continues to apply to a revocation made\nbefore the commencement as if the subsection had not been repealed.\n(5)\nIf subsection 20(7) or (8) of the old Act applied to 2 declarations (an\noriginal declaration and a fresh declaration) made before the\ncommencement, but the fresh declaration had not taken effect, and the\noriginal declaration had not ceased to have effect, under that subsection\nby the commencement, that subsection continues to apply to those\ndeclarations as if it had not been repealed.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments relating to the universal service regime"
    },
